{
  "title": "Clinical Research - SASH Vets",
  "text": "Clinical Research - SASH Vets\nSkip to main content\nSkip to footer\nOpens in a new tab\nVet Login\nFind your closest SASH vet\nEmergency Info\nCall SASH 24/7\nSearch ...\nSee all results\nOur Services\nDepartments\n24/7 Emergency\nAnaesthesia\nAvian and Exotics\nBehaviour\nCardiology\nCritical Care\nDentistry\nDermatology\nDiagnostic Imaging\nInternal Medicine\nNeurology & Neurosurgery\nOncology (Medical)\nOncology (Radiation)\nOncology (Surgical)\nOphthalmology\nPathology\nReproduction\nSports Medicine & Rehabilitation\nSurgery\nOther Services\nBlood Bank\nBladder & Kidney Centre\nCancer Centre\nClinical Research\nPituitary Centre\nRadioiodine\nTrauma Centre\nFacilities\nCT Scanner\nDialysis & Extracorporeal Therapies\nFluoroscopy\nHydrotherapy\nLinear Accelerator (LINAC)\nMRI Scanner\nTherapeutic Laser\nView All Services\nFor Pet Owners\nResources\nPet Advice & How tos\nDiseases, Conditions & Treatments\nPatient Stories\nInside SASH: The Specialist Vets\nVisiting SASH\nFees, Costs & Estimates\nPayment Options\nMeet the SASH Team\nBrowse SASH Services\nStray Animals Information\nFor Vets & Nurses\nResources\nOrder or Download SASH Marketing Materials\nCase Studies & Clinical Advice\nWhy SASH?\nClinical Research\nCE Programs\nCareers and Jobs at SASH\nVet Login/Refer Patient\nAbout SASH\nFor Media\nMedia Enquiries\nIn The Media\nAnnouncements\nAbout the SASH Network\nOur Team\nOur Locations\nOur Facilities\nCareers at SASH\nGovernance\nClinical Research\nMuch like clinical research in human medicine, veterinary clinical research is an essential part of improving future patient care and outcomes.\nHome\nServices\nClinical Research\nNorth Ryde\nWhy does SASH do clinical research?\nSASH is committed to providing the best quality care to pets and their owners\n.\nMuch like clinical research in human medicine, veterinary clinical research is an essential part of improving future patient care and outcomes. Many of the methods and treatments used at SASH, and other veterinary hospitals, have come from various forms of veterinary research.\nAlthough SASH practices today’s best available veterinary medicine, using the latest equipment, it is also expected that further improvements can be made through continuous research. Through research, we are able to identify the best tests and treatments for our much loved pets.\nSASH is the largest veterinary specialist hospital in Australia. We have the combined expertise of around 50 veterinary specialists including neurology, imaging, anaesthesia, critical care and rehabilitation, which are rarely found elsewhere.\nWith SASH’s dedication to high quality patient care and seeking out industry leading veterinarians and scientists from across the world, SASH is at the forefront of veterinary care. In turn, this attracts thousands of cases per month.\nWith the combination of the expertise of the SASH team and the high number of patients see, SASH is in a unique position to carry out no harm research. We aim to contribute to improving the care veterinarians can provide for pets throughout Australia.\nClinical research at SASH\nSASH conducts\nno harm\nresearch which is undertaken following ethics approval. The inclusion of patients in studies is on a voluntary basis and done following consultation and with the approval of pet owners.\nSASH’s primary duty is to pets and pet owners. As such, it is important to note that patient care is paramount and will\nalways\ntake precedence over research needs.\nSASH is accredited as a veterinary research establishment, and all prospective research is approved by an\nexternal\nethics committee.\nOur research is lead by\nDr Joanna White\n, who holds a PhD, a Masters of Veterinary Science majoring in Veterinary Epidemiology and is a registered Small Animal Internal Medicine Specialist.\nJoanna is experienced in research study design, has been published in a number of leading veterinary journals, is an examiner at Fellowship level for the Australasian College of Veterinary Scientists in both internal and feline medicine and is currently Australia’s representative on the International Renal Interest Society.\nResearch at SASH is supported by global animal health companies, such as IDEXX and charities such as the\nAustralian Companion Animal Health Foundation\n(ACAHF), part of the Australian Small\nAnimal Veterinary Association\nand the Australian College of Veterinary Science specialist’s training grants.\nExamples of SASH clinical research\nMedicine\nImproved use of antibiotics to treat urinary tract infections (cystitis) to guide clinical decision-making.\nInvestigating the link between age and risk of dehydration in cats. This may help reduce health issues associated with older cats during hot Australian summers.\nOptimising the use of radioactive iodine to treat hyperthryoidism, a very common hormonal problem in cats. This research aims to improve long term outcomes.\nDetermining the impact of general anaesthetic on kidney function of cats with chronic kidney disease.\nIdentifying risk factors associated with kidney stones, to help prevent this serious and painful condition in pets.\nSurgery\nWorld first research investigating the impact Double Pelvic Osteotomy (DPO), a form of surgery, for the treatment for canine hip dysplasia.\nRehabilitation\nUsing exercise tolerance testing as a predictor of quality of life and survival in cancer patients.\nOphthalmology\nThe use of how advanced imaging such as MRI and CT can be used to differentiate between causes of orbital disease, a condition that affects the eye socket.\nOncology\nThe use of a combination of two chemotherapy medications and its effects in treating aggressive mast cell tumours.\nOur Clinical Research Team\nFilter by Locations\nPerth\nWestern Sydney\nNorthern Beaches\nNorth Ryde\nSunshine Coast\nGold Coast\nAlexandria\nAdelaide\nCentral Coast\nView all team members\nDr Joanna White\nBVSc MVS(Epi) DAVCIM(SAIM) PhD\nSpecialist in Internal Medicine\nAvailable at\nNorth Ryde 24/7\n(02) 9889 0289\n1 Richardson Place,\nNorth Ryde NSW 2113\n1 Richardson Place,\nNorth Ryde, NSW 2113\nLocation Details\nOther Services at SASH\n24/7 Emergency Vet\nAnaesthesia\nAvian & Exotics\nBehaviour\nBladder and Kidney Centre\nBlood Bank\nCancer Centre\nCardiology\nClinical Research\nDentistry\nDermatology\nFeline Radioiodine\nHospital Care\nInternal Medicine\nMedical Oncology\nNeurology & Neurosurgery\nOphthalmology\nPathology\nPituitary Centre\nRadiation Oncology\nReproduction\nSports Medicine & Rehabilitation\nSurgery\nSurgical Oncology\nTrauma Centre\nVeterinary Intensive Care Unit (ICU)\nVeterinary Radiology & Diagnostic Imaging\nHelping pets and their families live their best lives.\nGet in touch\nCall SASH 24/7\nLocations\nOpening Hours\nMonday - 24 hours\nTuesday - 24 hours\nWednesday - 24 hours\nThursday - 24 hours\nFriday - 24 hours\nSaturday - 24 hours\nSunday - 24 hours\nSASH Vets\nOur Services\nOur Facilities\nOur Locations\nOur Team\nOur Governance\nMedia Enquiries\nContact Us\nFor Pet Owners\nPet Advice & How tos\nDiseases, Conditions & Treatments\nPatient Stories\nInside SASH: The Specialist Vets\nFor Vets & Nurses\nContinued Education (CE)\nCase Studies & Clinical Advice\nCareers for Vets & Nurses\nVet Login Portal\nLocations\nAdelaide 24/7\nAlexandria 24/7\nCentral Coast 24/7\nGold Coast 24/7\nNorth Ryde 24/7\nNorthern Beaches 24/7\nSunshine Coast 24/7\nPerth 24/7\nOpening November 9th!\nWestern Sydney 24/7\nSASH acknowledges Traditional Owners of Country throughout Australia and recognises the continuing connection to lands, waters, and communities. We pay our respect to Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander cultures; and to Elders past and present.\nOur Services\nOur Services\n24/7 Emergency Hospital\nVeterinary Surgery\nInternal Medicine\nDEPARTMENTS\n24/7 Emergency Vet\nAnaesthesia\nAvian & Exotics\nBehaviour\nCardiology\nDentistry\nDermatology\nInternal Medicine\nMedical Oncology\nNeurology & Neurosurgery\nOphthalmology\nPathology\nRadiation Oncology\nReproduction\nSports Medicine & Rehabilitation\nSurgery\nSurgical Oncology\nVeterinary Intensive Care Unit (ICU)\nVeterinary Radiology & Diagnostic Imaging\nADDITIONAL SERVICES\nBladder and Kidney Centre\nBlood Bank\nCancer Centre\nClinical Research\nFeline Radioiodine\nPituitary Centre\nTrauma Centre\nFacilities\nCT Scanner\nDialysis & Extracorporeal Therapies\nFluoroscopy\nHydrotherapy\nMedical Linear Accelerator (LINAC)\nMRI for Animals\nTherapeutic Laser\nFor Pet Owners\nFor Pet Owners\nVisiting SASH\nFees, Costs & Estimates\nPayment Options\nBrowse SASH Services\n24/7 Emergency Hospital\nStray Animals Information\nRESOURCES\nPet Advice & How tos\nDiseases, Conditions & Treatments\nPatient Stories\nInside SASH: The Specialist Vets\nFor Vets & Nurses\nFor Vets & Nurses\nCE Programs\nCareers and Jobs at SASH\nRefer a Patient & Vet Login\nRESOURCES\nOrder or Download SASH Marketing Materials\nCase Studies & Clinical Advice\nWhy SASH\nClinical Research\nAbout SASH\nAbout SASH\nAbout the SASH Network\nOur Team\nOur Locations\nOur Facilities\nCareers at SASH\nGovernance\nFor Media\nMedia Enquiries\nIn The Media\nAnnouncements\nPOPULAR\nFees, Costs and Estimates\nMeet the SASH Team\nCareers\nContact Us\nMedia Enquiries\n© 2026 Small Animal Specialist Hospital. All Rights Reserved.\nPrivacy Policy\n.\nLegal & Disclaimer\n.\nSitemap\n. Built by\nStudio Twofold\n.\nSearch SASH\nSearch ...\nSearch\nSee all results\nPopular Searches include:",
